# Feature Change Documentation

- Document every feature addition, feature update, bug fix, and functionality change in `docs/changelog.md` at the repository root.
- Add each changelog entry with the date, change type, a concise summary, and any relevant user or developer impact.
- When a feature or existing behavior changes, update `docs/docs.md` in the same change so its descriptions, examples, navigation, and current-state notes remain accurate.
- Keep `docs/docs.md` aligned with the implemented behavior; do not leave documentation describing removed, renamed, or obsolete functionality.
- Create `docs/changelog.md` if it does not exist, and preserve the existing entry format when adding to it.
- Treat documentation updates as part of the feature, fix, or functionality change rather than as optional follow-up work.
